{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"3054","artifact_type":"feature-context","name":"plan/feature-context-3054-architecture-drift-audit.md@sha256:b91b6edd2d09143f53f5efc467febb3d7f0ca91195f72b6b9b74673ef4174d1e"},"owner_reference":"3054","content":"# ARTIFACT:DISCOVERY\n\n## Feature\n\ndocs: per-module architecture refresh, concept consolidation, and documentation-versus-behaviour drift audit\n\n## Problem Statement\n\nThe plugin's documentation does not describe its own structure. There is no component map. Eight code packages exist (agent_profile, backlog_core, dh_core, dispatch_schema, hooks, progressive_markdown, sam_schema, scripts); exactly one had an ARCHITECTURE.md before this session. Nothing stated what each package owns, consumes, or where near-duplicates diverge. Consequence, demonstrated repeatedly in the originating session: agents generalize incorrectly from whichever package they land in first.\n\n## Goals\n\n- Every code package has an architecture description: role, owns, consumes, consumed-by, detail location\n- Near-collisions between modules/concepts carry explicit distinction notes\n- Concepts/glossary consolidated to one definition each, others link rather than restate\n- Shared root path and naming convention defined and documented\n- Drift audit complete: every plugin document fact-checked against code, workflow, and prose behaviour\n- Drift review chart produced supporting all three adjudication outcomes, reviewed\n- Cross-reference table produced identifying every multi-document topic and its duplicate sources\n- Resulting material reachable from the plugin's discovery index, not orphaned\n\n## Expected Behavior\n\nAs an agent or contributor working anywhere in the development-harness plugin, an authoritative per-module architecture description, a consolidated concept glossary, and a verified record of where documentation and behaviour disagree exist, so the right component and the right detail can be found without inferring the system's shape from whichever file was opened first.\n\n## Desired Structure\n\nRequired deliverables, per the item body: (1) per-module architecture and relationships for every code package with explicit distinction notes on near-collisions; (2) authoritative concept consolidation and glossary, one definition per concept; (3) structure design at a shared root path with documented naming convention; (4) documentation-versus-behaviour drift audit producing a review chart supporting three adjudication outcomes (docs wrong, code wrong, neither matches desired architecture); (5) cross-reference and duplicate-source table for every multi-document topic.\n\n## Progress Since Item Creation (session context as of this grooming pass)\n\nThis item was filed as the deferred, systematic follow-on to a narrower, now largely-complete pass: the markdown-consumption architecture work (contract R1-R8, component-architecture.md, CONTEXT.md/CONTEXT-MAP.md, five ADRs) is substantially done on PR #3080, having gone through three full review rounds (Greptile automated review, a dispatched peer session's feasibility check against actual code, and direct code verification of every load-bearing claim). Eight gap issues (#3057-#3064) plus five decision issues (#3072-#3076, all resolved) plus four issues discovered during verification (#3078, #3079, #3081, #3082) are filed and cross-referenced. This item's own \"Architecture Baseline\" and \"Gap Items\" sections are themselves now somewhat stale relative to that progress (they predate PR #3080's three review rounds) \u2014 the drift-audit and concept-consolidation work this item scopes has not yet started; only its stated prerequisite (the narrower markdown-consumption pass) has.\n\n## Open Questions\n\n- None from a discovery standpoint \u2014 this item's scope, deliverables, and rationale are already fully specified in its own body. The grooming pass proceeding from this artifact should focus on RT-ICA/fact-check/impact-analysis of readiness to start, not requirements gathering."}